From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AsteroidOS <pike@asteroidos>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 04:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] backports: drop duplicate bit_wait_io (pike oreo kernel has it)

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [backports/vendor-kernel symbol collision]

pike's 3.10-oreo kernel already defines bit_wait_io in kernel/wait.c, so the
backports 3.17 compat copy causes a multiple-definition link error in vmlinux.
bit_wait and ktime_get_raw are absent from pike's kernel, so they remain.
---
--- a/backports/compat/backport-3.17.c
+++ b/backports/compat/backport-3.17.c
@@ -19,13 +19,6 @@
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(bit_wait);
 
-int bit_wait_io(void *word)
-{
-	io_schedule();
-	return 0;
-}
-EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(bit_wait_io);
-
 /**
  * ktime_get_raw - Returns the raw monotonic time in ktime_t format
  */
